WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Who are spies? They are the best actors in the world.

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.080
They live someone else's life.

3
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.660
They have ten names, ten passports and ten identities.

4
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.860
Everything we know about them we know from movies,

5
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:15.400
but we also know that every state has its own spies, secret security agents.

6
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.320
Besides having a gift for being the best actors in the world,

7
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:23.140
they use tools that let them hear everything, see everything and be anyone.

8
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.400
In today's video I'm testing spy tools that will help me

9
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.180
hear everything, see everything, get in anywhere

10
00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.700
and in the end become anyone.

11
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.240
Even now I don't recognize what this is...

12
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.340
Oh my, you look like nothing.

13
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.700
Look like him or not — I'm looking at him.

14
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.160
To become a spy, I first need to be a very good actor,

15
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.060
but I'll only be able to test that at the end of the video.

16
00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:48.540
And for now, to begin with, I have to learn to eavesdrop on conversations unnoticed.

17
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.280
The first tool I'm using is a bugging flash drive.

18
00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.020
On the outside it looks like a perfectly ordinary flash drive,

19
00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:56.380
but inside you have a microphone and an SD card slot.

20
00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.220
So when you turn it on, it records everything around.

21
00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.360
So now we move on to the first test.

22
00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:04.640
I told Anđela that I hid a hidden microphone somewhere in the room.

23
00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:08.060
And asked her to sit alone in the room and say whatever she wants.

24
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.040
Let's see whether the flash drive records everything she said.

25
00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:16.100
The problem with Aleksa's room is that there are lots of things here that look like a microphone.

26
00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.820
Maybe on the shelf, because there are really many things there.

27
00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:25.240
So, first tell me, what do you think is the microphone in the room?

28
00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:26.460
This flash drive.

29
00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.600
Now let's see whether this flash drive really recorded what Anđela said.

30
00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:33.600
Did you hear how this microphone, that is, this flash drive, records?

31
00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:34.720
Honestly — 9 out of 10.

32
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.280
It sounds great, and it's really hard to notice.

33
00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:39.680
The only reason it's 9 out of 10 and not 10 out of 10 —

34
00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.140
is because it says "voice recorder" here.

35
00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.180
The next spy tool is a GPS tracker and bug.

36
00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:49.020
First let's check how it works as a bug.

37
00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:54.100
You literally take off this cover, and an SD card and a SIM card are inserted inside.

38
00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.520
And how do we actually eavesdrop with this device?

39
00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.620
All you need is the phone number of the card we inserted inside...

40
00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.480
just call that number.

41
00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:10.080
And this number answers automatically, and we can eavesdrop on someone.

42
00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.620
And now let's see whether we can follow someone.

43
00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:15.280
Come on, swing by for a minute, give me a ride to the store.

44
00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.360
I asked David to drive us to the store.

45
00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:19.960
And I secretly attached this tracker to his car.

46
00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:21.900
Let's see where he goes after that.

47
00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:25.740
Let's now take a look, just to hear what it sounds like when you call it.

48
00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.740
And now let's see how I can track where the car is.

49
00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:32.380
You send the message "999,"

50
00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:36.840
and right after that you get a link to Google Maps.

51
00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:40.700
David is at the back entrance of the café where he works.

52
00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:43.240
So now we know where David went to work.

53
00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:46.480
Besides the tool with which you can find out where the car is,

54
00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:49.420
there's also a tool with which you can find out everything about that car.

55
00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:53.400
carVertical is an app made for anyone who wants to buy a new car

56
00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.960
or wants to find out as much as possible about their vehicle.

57
00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.580
If we really find the car we're following,

58
00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:00.480
then, like real agents, we'll learn all the information about it too.

59
00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.780
His car should be parked down here.

60
00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:04.540
Are my eyes deceiving me?

61
00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:06.460
There, folks, David's car is here.

62
00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:07.760
We found David's car.

63
00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.260
This thing survived the road.

64
00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.540
And now let's see how carVertical works.

65
00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:15.120
With carVertical all you need is to enter the car's chassis number.

66
00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.720
And that way you can check which country the car was imported from,

67
00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.260
whether it was ever in an accident,

68
00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.680
whether the mileage was rolled back,

69
00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:21.820
how many owners it had

70
00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:23.840
and most importantly — whether it was ever stolen.

71
00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.920
Hey, Daki, come here, I need to show you something.

72
00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:27.800
You open the carVertical app

73
00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:30.220
and here you enter your chassis number.

74
00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:33.460
David, it says here that your car has driven 426,000 km.

75
00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:35.460
And my odometer says 250.

76
00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:37.780
426,000.

77
00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:38.820
426,000.

78
00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.360
So they rolled back your mileage.

79
00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:43.680
And second: your car is damaged at the rear.

80
00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.200
Did you damage it or someone else?

81
00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:45.920
Me, me.

82
00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:46.920
You damaged it.

83
00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:47.540
Let's see.

84
00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.160
Damage amounting to between 60,000 and 180,000 dinars.

85
00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:52.680
Let's look at the car's specifications too.

86
00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:54.180
Peugeot 206, 1.4.

87
00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:55.160
Diesel, manual transmission.

88
00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.000
Bravo, bravo.

89
00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:56.800
That's all correct.

90
00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.740
With carVertical you can knock down the price of the car you're buying,

91
00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.060
and also save money because you don't need to bring a mechanic.

92
00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.780
Really, for what carVertical offers, the price is small anyway.

93
00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:08.700
But if you enter the code NOTALEKSA, you get another 30% off the price.

94
00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.940
And note, you pay only when you check a car.

95
00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:12.880
No monthly charges and so on.

96
00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.100
The carVertical link is in the description of this video,

97
00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.060
and I suggest that for safety reasons

98
00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:18.720
you check the car you already have too.

99
00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.880
The rating for this GPS tracker is 7 out of 10,

100
00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.460
the battery could last a bit longer,

101
00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:25.160
and the rating for carVertical is, of course, 10 out of 10.

102
00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:29.000
If I can follow someone with these amateur tools and they don't know it,

103
00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.260
imagine what real spies can do.

104
00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.860
And there are also hidden cameras in a pencil,

105
00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.940
in the shape of a shirt button, in the shape of glasses,

106
00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.960
but they all work on the same principle.

107
00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.940
You charge it, turn it on, insert an SD card,

108
00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:43.260
connect to Wi-Fi and hide it anywhere.

109
00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:45.540
Okay, folks, I hid a hidden camera here.

110
00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.460
I bought Anđela's favorite chips

111
00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:48.920
and put them on the table.

112
00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:50.440
Now she'll come into the room,

113
00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:51.840
and I'll, like, go out somewhere,

114
00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.860
and we'll see whether she steals my chips

115
00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.640
and whether the camera catches her.

116
00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.740
Sit here for a minute, I'll go film something over there in the kitchen.

117
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.940
I need it for the next scene, just wait for me.

118
00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:02.560
Okay, folks, there,

119
00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:04.240
we're now in another room.

120
00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:07.100
I think she noticed the chips.

121
00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:07.580
There.

122
00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:13.530
I knew she'd take them.

123
00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:16.670
Okay, Anči, since I know you ate my chips,

124
00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:20.630
I'll just tell you there's a hidden camera somewhere in this room.

125
00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:24.090
By the way, this hidden camera films in pitch darkness too.

126
00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:25.910
Now we'll make Anđela

127
00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:28.650
find the hidden camera in pitch darkness.

128
00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:30.570
This is our next spy tool.

129
00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:33.150
It's a hidden camera detector.

130
00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:36.290
It's literally a lens you look through,

131
00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:40.650
and when you turn it on, it reflects infrared light,

132
00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:45.090
and through this lens you can find where the camera is hidden.

133
00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:48.330
And you'll look through it, and in pitch darkness

134
00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:50.330
try to find where the hidden camera is.

135
00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:53.490
Meanwhile the camera is filming in night mode, that is, in the dark.

136
00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:56.830
But you can see that infrared light is reflecting somewhere.

137
00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:58.110
Aha, what did you see?

138
00:05:58.450 --> 00:05:58.850
There it is.

139
00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:04.190
Anyway, folks, Anđela successfully found the camera with this tool,

140
00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:05.550
so it's proven: it works.

141
00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.810
You can use it for personal safety,

142
00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:09.550
to find out whether someone is spying on you,

143
00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:11.550
whether someone has placed a hidden camera somewhere.

144
00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.990
There are quite a few cases where someone goes to an Airbnb

145
00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:17.410
or an apartment from Booking to spend the night,

146
00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:21.310
and the owners put hidden cameras in a charger,

147
00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:23.770
in a clock, an alarm clock, in some lamp.

148
00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:28.150
So this is a must-have, rating 10 out of 10, definitely.

149
00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.630
And the camera filmed what Anđela was doing well even in pitch darkness,

150
00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:33.250
and caught her stealing my chips,

151
00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:37.810
but the quality somehow falls short of today's standards.

152
00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:39.970
Rating 7 out of 10.

153
00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:42.370
The next tool is what hunters use,

154
00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:43.870
and also special forces.

155
00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:46.470
These are night vision goggles.

156
00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:49.210
And literally with them you can move around in the dark

157
00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:50.510
and still see perfectly.

158
00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:52.730
Now I'll turn off all the lights in my room,

159
00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:56.210
then Anđela will hide these three yellow ducklings,

160
00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:59.530
and I'll try to find all three ducklings with this gadget.

161
00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:00.890
Okay, here we go.

162
00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:06.770
The room is pitch dark, but there's an outlet over there.

163
00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:10.410
By the way, this thing zooms in a lot, and you can't zoom out all the way.

164
00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:11.610
Wait, let's look on the shelf.

165
00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:14.130
No, no.

166
00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:16.030
Aha.

167
00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.650
Look where she put one.

168
00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:21.630
By the way, this is my lizard Lizzy,

169
00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:25.510
and Anđela, in his terrarium, next to Lizzy,

170
00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:28.330
put one duckling.

171
00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:31.150
Aha.

172
00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:32.730
And here's the second one.

173
00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:35.550
She literally put it in my bed.

174
00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:37.690
Right next to the pillow.

175
00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:38.850
This, folks, is the second duckling.

176
00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:39.930
Now to find the last one too.

177
00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:42.170
Ah, time's up.

178
00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:44.870
I managed to find only two ducklings.

179
00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:49.390
Do you know how I struggled to find it?

180
00:07:49.390 --> 00:07:50.470
And how do you think

181
00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:52.390
I know you're not subscribed to the channel?

182
00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:55.390
Besides the fact that more than 90% of you actually aren't subscribed,

183
00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:56.670
I'm also watching you.

184
00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:57.810
Subscribe to my channel,

185
00:07:57.950 --> 00:07:59.910
that way you definitely won't miss future videos,

186
00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:01.910
and we're only a tiny bit away from 50,000.

187
00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:04.290
Real spies, besides tools for eavesdropping,

188
00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:05.450
surveillance and location tracking,

189
00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:07.310
must master one skill.

190
00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.990
And that's the skill of picking locks.

191
00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:12.830
And in order to learn to open any lock

192
00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:13.750
that we'll face,

193
00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:15.730
we need to know how a lock works.

194
00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.570
This is the simplest example of a padlock,

195
00:08:17.570 --> 00:08:20.790
and here you can see that when the key enters the keyhole,

196
00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:23.970
it actually moves these pins inside.

197
00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:26.230
So, the key is made with uneven cuts,

198
00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:29.230
so these pins of different sizes

199
00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:32.530
line up when the key enters.

200
00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:33.810
And when they line up,

201
00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.970
we can turn the cylinder inside without any problem.

202
00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:39.670
And now — how do we line up all these pins

203
00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:41.090
without a key?

204
00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:43.850
This isn't actually a real lock pick,

205
00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:45.450
it's a tool for repairing locks.

206
00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:48.390
The first one clicked, the second one clicked,

207
00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:51.370
the third is in place,

208
00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.570
the fourth doesn't move,

209
00:08:53.570 --> 00:09:00.780
and when the fourth and fifth click,

210
00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:05.780
you literally open the lock without a key.

211
00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:07.780
But this is a practice lock,

212
00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:10.020
and when you see what's happening inside,

213
00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:10.700
it's much easier.

214
00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:13.220
Here we have locks of different difficulty,

215
00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:14.780
and at the end we have a real

216
00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.740
lock, one that actually

217
00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:19.440
is installed in many apartments and houses.

218
00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:21.540
The kind people install and consider

219
00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:22.980
the most reliable locks.

220
00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:29.420
We managed to open this little lock,

221
00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:31.920
the kind usually used to lock backpacks,

222
00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.300
suitcases and so on.

223
00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:42.480
Without much trouble

224
00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.120
we managed to open a cheap Chinese lock.

225
00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:48.040
This time I'm applying tension from the bottom side,

226
00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:51.000
because that way it might be easier for me

227
00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:53.700
to reach the pins.

228
00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:57.640
And there, a piece of cake.

229
00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:00.340
We opened almost all the padlocks.

230
00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:02.040
And what about real locks?

231
00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:04.320
These locks are supposed to protect

232
00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:07.140
your apartment, your house from burglars.

233
00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:08.320
But let's see

234
00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:11.040
whether they are really that good.

235
00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:21.680
So now we're sure we have this skill —

236
00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.920
like a real spy, to get in anywhere.

237
00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:26.420
But how do I become anyone?

238
00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:28.600
This time I'd like to become

239
00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:29.400
an old man.

240
00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.020
David is a man who has known me for more than 10 years.

241
00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:34.140
But will I be able to disguise myself as an old man,

242
00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:35.840
come to his store,

243
00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:36.900
ask him for something —

244
00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:38.840
and have him not realize it's me?

245
00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:40.960
So, to disguise myself, I bought all this.

246
00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:42.520
First, here we have liquid latex,

247
00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:44.540
which is used to change skin texture

248
00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.920
and make all kinds of shapes and so on.

249
00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:48.440
Anyway, a very good thing

250
00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:51.140
if you want to make skin look like an old man's.

251
00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:52.640
The second thing is this wax

252
00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:54.440
for special effects makeup,

253
00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:55.460
for film makeup.

254
00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:57.720
It literally looks like plasticine,

255
00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.220
which you soften with paraffin,

256
00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:01.440
and you can sculpt different shapes from it,

257
00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:03.180
